00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:14,740
This is an email I got recently said this:

155
00:07:14,740 --> 00:07:18,740
We recently had a ceremony for a scout

156
00:07:18,740 --> 00:07:21,740
who had turned 18 years old without becoming an Eagle Scout

157
00:07:21,740 --> 00:07:24,740
but was going to move on to become an adult volunteer.

158
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:27,740
Several people mentioned to me in passing

159
00:07:27,740 --> 00:07:31,740
that it was a terrible shame that the scout never got Eagle.

160
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:35,740
And it was a terrible shame that the scout never got Eagle

161
00:07:35,740 --> 00:07:38,740
And kind of thought it was a terrible waste of time.

162
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:40,740
I thought they were dead wrong

163
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:42,740
and I felt a little insulted.

164
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:46,740
Scout I'm talking about has done a lot of really great things,

165
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:50,740
is really a great guy, spent a lot of time in scouts,

166
00:07:50,740 --> 00:07:52,740
wasn't very interested in becoming an Eagle

167
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:55,740
And to call what he did in scouting a waste of time

168
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:57,740
bothers me a little bit.

169
00:07:57,740 --> 00:07:59,740
If we're just concentrating on getting Eagle,

170
00:07:59,740 --> 00:08:02,740
we're missing the fact that there's a whole lot more

171
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:04,740
a young person you can get out of scouting

172
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:09,740
Down the road. another troop just awarded a 13-year-old Eagle

173
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:12,740
And there were high fives and kudos passed around.

174
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:16,740
But I beg to ask you which scouting career was more successful.

175
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:19,740
Well, I'm going to agree with you almost.

176
00:08:19,740 --> 00:08:22,740
oh, I guess maybe about 80%,

177
00:08:22,740 --> 00:08:25,740
And my answer might sound a little snotty

178
00:08:25,740 --> 00:08:28,740
And I apologize if it does.

179
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:31,740
I guess it just kind of comes with the territory sometimes,

180
00:08:31,740 --> 00:08:32,740
But really no,

181
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:34,740
I'm intending this in the best way possible.

182
00:08:34,740 --> 00:08:37,740
First, people have this overblown attitude

183
00:08:37,740 --> 00:08:39,740
towards becoming an Eagle,

184
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:40,740
And I get that.

185
00:08:40,740 --> 00:08:43,740
I wish they would understand that there are a lot of scouts

186
00:08:43,740 --> 00:08:45,740
who can get a great deal out of scouting

187
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:48,740
without ever wanting to become an Eagle Scout.

188
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:51,740
You know, it's a great achievement, sure,

189
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:53,740
But not everybody's interested in it.

190
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:55,740
And if people don't get it-

191
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:57,740
but not everybody's interested in it,

192
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,740
And if people did understand that

193
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:02,740
they wouldn't stand around and kind of say under the breath,

194
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,740
wow, it's just a dirty shame,

195
00:09:04,740 --> 00:09:06,740
and boy didn't get to be an Eagle Scout.

196
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:07,740
Maybe he wasn't interested,

197
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:09,740
Maybe it meant nothing to him,

198
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:11,740
Maybe what was important to him,

199
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:13,740
what he was doing in scouts.

200
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:15,740
But I got to tell you, friend,

201
00:09:15,740 --> 00:09:17,740
you're kind of doing the same thing

202
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:20,740
in trying to draw a comparison between this scout

203
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,740
and the 13-year-old Eagle Scout,

204
00:09:22,740 --> 00:09:24,740
Because it kind of sounds like

205
00:09:24,740 --> 00:09:26,740
you think the 13-year-old Eagle Scout

206
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,740
wasn't as successful as this scout.

207
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:31,740
And this was what really takes me to the part

208
00:09:31,740 --> 00:09:34,740
where I'm going to be a little snotty. okay,

209
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,740
These kind of comparisons,

210
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:38,740
these apple and orange comparisons,

211
00:09:38,740 --> 00:09:40,740
aren't proper in any way that we do them.

212
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:43,740
You're asking me to give you an opinion

213
00:09:43,740 --> 00:09:46,740
based on two incomparable things,

214
00:09:46,740 --> 00:09:48,740
And at the heart of that matter

215
00:09:48,740 --> 00:09:51,740
lies a whole lot of things. that kind of dog us in scouting.

216
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:53,740
You know in the way that we look at things

217
00:09:53,740 --> 00:09:55,740
and the way we consider things.

218
00:09:55,740 --> 00:09:57,740
So let me explain myself.

219
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:59,740
In drawing a comparison between those two scouts,

220
00:09:59,740 --> 00:10:01,740
you're kind of asking which is the best fruit,

221
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:03,740
an orange or an apple?

222
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:05,740
Now, I like oranges, okay,

223
00:10:05,740 --> 00:10:07,740
But you know, not all that often

224
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:08,740
Apples are great.

225
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:10,740
I probably like them more. all right,

226
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:11,740
To be honest with you,

227
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:12,740
I don't know about you,

228
00:10:12,740 --> 00:10:14,740
but if somebody offered me the choice

229
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:15,740
of an apple or an orange,

230
00:10:15,740 --> 00:10:17,740
I'd probably take the apple seven times out of ten,

231
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:19,740
unless I was kind of in an orange mood,

232
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:21,740
if you know what I'm talking about.

233
00:10:21,740 --> 00:10:23,740
Now, if somebody else chose the orange,

234
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:25,740
well, I wouldn't get all worked up about it

235
00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:27,740
and try to explain why the apple was so much better,

236
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:30,740
because I don't have to eat what they chose, right,

237
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:32,740
I get to eat my apple.

238
00:10:32,740 --> 00:10:34,740
Now, no matter how hard you try to make

239
00:10:34,740 --> 00:10:37,740
every apple or orange the same as all the others,

240
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:40,740
each one's got to be a little bit different, right?

241
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,740
It'd be pretty boring eating identical apples

242
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:44,740
or oranges all the time. anyway,

243
00:10:44,740 --> 00:10:46,740
No matter how hard you try,

244
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:48,740
you can't make an apple into an orange

245
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:49,740
or vice versa.

246
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:52,740
So that kind of leads to the question:

247
00:10:52,740 --> 00:10:54,740
are all scouts the same?

248
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:55,740
No, they're not,

249
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:57,740
Not by a long shot, right?

250
00:10:57,740 --> 00:10:59,740
Are all eagle scouts exactly the same?

251
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,740
No, they're not,

252
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:01,740
Not by a long shot.

253
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:05,740
Do I care if a scout achieves eagle?

254
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,740
No, actually not really.

255
00:11:07,740 --> 00:11:09,740
I mean, it's something great to do,

256
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:11,740
but not everybody's all that interested in it.

257
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:14,740
Do I care how old a scout is

258
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:16,740
when they achieve eagle?

259
00:11:16,740 --> 00:11:18,740
No, I don't.

260
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,740
Well, look honestly, really I do.

261
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:22,740
I would prefer they were younger

262
00:11:22,740 --> 00:11:25,740
than 17 years, 11 months and 28 days,

263
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:27,740
but you know, I've learned

264
00:11:27,740 --> 00:11:30,740
that you don't always get what you want. okay,

265
00:11:30,740 --> 00:11:32,740
You know I serve three or four more times

266
00:11:32,740 --> 00:11:34,740
as long as a scout master than most people do.

267
00:11:34,740 --> 00:11:36,740
Does that make me something special?

268
00:11:36,740 --> 00:11:38,740
No, not really.

269
00:11:38,740 --> 00:11:40,740
I just manage to stay around longer,

270
00:11:40,740 --> 00:11:41,740
That's all

271
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:43,740
I mean. you see where I'm headed here.

272
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:45,740
The kind of comparisons that we often draw

273
00:11:45,740 --> 00:11:49,740
as scouters is- wait for it-

274
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:51,740
apples and oranges.

275
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:53,740
They're just things that they're.

276
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:56,740
well, I love it. a good idiom, okay.

277
00:11:56,740 --> 00:11:58,740
And the idiom of comparing apples to oranges

278
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:01,740
refers to the apparent differences

279
00:12:01,740 --> 00:12:04,740
between things that are incomparable

280
00:12:04,740 --> 00:12:07,740
or inco-measurable.

281
00:12:07,740 --> 00:12:09,740
It's a false analogy, like saying

282
00:12:09,740 --> 00:12:11,740
an apple is not a good orange.

283
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,740
And I love a good idiom

284
00:12:14,740 --> 00:12:16,740
And this one's a doozy right.

285
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:17,740
You know, in much of Europe

286
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:18,740
when they use this idiom

287
00:12:18,740 --> 00:12:20,740
they say apples and pears,

288
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:21,740
And in Latin America

289
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,740
it's potatoes and sweet potatoes,

290
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:27,740
Believe it or not. in Serbia, okay,

291
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:30,740
They say comparing grandmothers and toads.

292
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:34,740
In Romania they compare cows to longjons.

293
00:12:34,740 --> 00:12:36,740
The Welsh compare honey and butter,

294
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:39,740
And there's a Danish idiom that I really like:

295
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:40,740
What is highest,

296
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:44,740
A roundtower or a thunderclap?

297
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:47,740
In Russia they compare warm and soft.

298
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:48,740
In Poland they ask

299
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:50,740
what is gingerbread to a widnall?

300
00:12:50,740 --> 00:12:51,740
I mean really,

301
00:12:51,740 --> 00:12:52,740
Rather than asking

302
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:54,740
who's the most successful scout,

303
00:12:54,740 --> 00:12:55,740
How about if we ask

304
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:57,740
if that particular young person

305
00:12:57,740 --> 00:12:59,740
got something out of being a scout?

306
00:12:59,740 --> 00:13:01,740
There's no comparison in the scout oath.

307
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:03,740
It only uses personal pronouns.

308
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:05,740
On my honor,

309
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:09,740
I will do my best.

310
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:12,740
So when people want to draw comparisons like this,

311
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:14,740
or they want to say:

312
00:13:14,740 --> 00:13:16,740
you know, this guy didn't get eagle

313
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,740
and compared to the other guys that got eagle,

314
00:13:18,740 --> 00:13:19,740
well, that's kind of a waste.

315
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:20,740
It's a dirty shame that he did.

316
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:22,740
Oh, come on people,

317
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:24,740
Really No.

318
00:13:24,740 --> 00:13:25,740
How about we guide our scouts

319
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:28,740
to evaluate themselves against themselves

320
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,740
On my honor.

321
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:32,740
I will do my best,

322
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:34,740
Not everybody else's best.

323
00:13:34,740 --> 00:13:36,740
I'm going to do the best that I can possibly do.

324
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:38,740
Wouldn't that be good?

325
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:40,740
I mean, isn't that a more useful thing

326
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:41,740
to be able to do?

327
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,740
Isn't that a more useful life skill?

328
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,740
How about we get them in the habit of doing that?

329
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:49,740
I think that would keep our eye more on the ball,

330
00:13:49,740 --> 00:13:50,740
don't you think?

331
00:13:50,740 --> 00:13:53,740
And we can leave the immeasurable comparisons

332
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:55,740
of apples and oranges and toads

333
00:13:55,740 --> 00:13:59,740
and grandmothers and all that kind of thing

334
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:01,740
to somebody else.

335
00:14:01,740 --> 00:14:04,740
This next email came to me from Brian Kerner.

336
00:14:04,740 --> 00:14:06,740
Pretty quick question:

337
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:09,740
Can a scout hold the same position of responsibility

338
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:12,740
from first class all the way through life rank?

339
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:14,740
I'm not saying it's a good practice,

340
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:16,740
I'm just curious if it's allowed.

341
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:18,740
Well, Brian, these kind of questions come up

342
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:19,740
from time to time

343
00:14:19,740 --> 00:14:21,740
and it's really easy to get an answer for it.

344
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:23,740
I don't even have to really tell you the answer,

345
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:26,740
because the answer is in the requirement.

346
00:14:26,740 --> 00:14:28,740
If there was such a restriction-

347
00:14:28,740 --> 00:14:31,740
if, for instance, a scout could not be credited

348
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:34,740
for the same position of responsibility

349
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:37,740
for different ranks- it would very clearly say so

350
00:14:37,740 --> 00:14:39,740
within the requirement.

351
00:14:39,740 --> 00:14:41,740
So let's talk about this for a moment.

352
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:43,740
Positions of responsibility are all listed

353
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,740
in the requirements for first class

354
00:14:45,740 --> 00:14:47,740
star, life and eagle.

355
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:49,740
The list is a little bit different for eagle,

356
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:51,740
but it's the same for first class

357
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:52,740
star and life.

358
00:14:52,740 --> 00:14:55,740
There is a number of months of tenure

359
00:14:55,740 --> 00:14:57,740
you have to serve successfully

360
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,740
in a position of responsibility to qualify

361
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:00,740
for those ranks,

362
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,740
And those months can be served

363
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:04,740
non-consecutively.

364
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:06,740
They can be served in one position

365
00:15:06,740 --> 00:15:09,740
or in a combination of positions of responsibility.

366
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:10,740
So there you have it.

367
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:12,740
It's really pretty simple,

368
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:13,740
but it's a good question

369
00:15:13,740 --> 00:15:14,740
and I appreciate getting it.

370
